1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,955
Welcome to Module 5, all about
calendars and online booking!

2
00:00:03,955 --> 00:00:07,640
Before we build one, let's look
at the different calendar types,

3
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:11,671
so you can pick the right one for
every kind of appointment you offer.

4
00:00:12,526 --> 00:00:15,416
Calendars have their own
place in the sidebar.

5
00:00:15,416 --> 00:00:19,877
The Calendar Settings tab lists every
booking calendar in your account.

6
00:00:19,877 --> 00:00:23,145
Bloom Dental already has
7, and each one has a type.

7
00:00:23,145 --> 00:00:25,784
The type decides who gets booked, and how.

8
00:00:26,634 --> 00:00:30,791
When you click Create Calendar, the
first thing you choose is the type.

9
00:00:30,791 --> 00:00:34,597
Let's go through each one, with
a real example from the practice.

10
00:00:34,597 --> 00:00:39,398
Take a moment over this choice, because
the type is the one thing you can't change

11
00:00:39,398 --> 00:00:39,749
later.

12
00:00:40,601 --> 00:00:44,966
A Personal Booking calendar books
time with one specific person.

13
00:00:44,966 --> 00:00:49,331
Bloom uses one for implant
consultations, which only Sarah does.

14
00:00:49,331 --> 00:00:52,810
Patients see Sarah's free
times, and nobody else's.

15
00:00:53,661 --> 00:00:56,504
Round Robin shares bookings across a team.

16
00:00:56,504 --> 00:00:59,483
A check-up can be done
by James or by Priya,

17
00:00:59,483 --> 00:01:02,190
so each booking goes to whoever is free.

18
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:06,929
You can also balance the bookings
evenly, or give one person priority.

19
00:01:07,778 --> 00:01:13,150
Class Booking is for groups: one host,
many attendees, and a set number of seats.

20
00:01:13,150 --> 00:01:16,135
Bloom's Invisalign open
evening has 12 seats,

21
00:01:16,135 --> 00:01:19,252
and bookings stop
automatically when it's full.

22
00:01:20,102 --> 00:01:24,581
Collective Booking only offers a time
when everyone you select is free.

23
00:01:24,581 --> 00:01:29,250
For a smile makeover planning session,
Sarah and Priya must both be there,

24
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:32,909
so Kyntlo only shows the slots
that work for both of them.

25
00:01:33,760 --> 00:01:37,872
A Service Menu lets clients choose
a service first, like a scan,

26
00:01:37,872 --> 00:01:40,635
a clean or whitening,
and then pick a time.

27
00:01:40,635 --> 00:01:43,784
Each service has its own
length and its own team.

28
00:01:43,784 --> 00:01:46,675
It's ideal when you
offer lots of treatments.

29
00:01:47,526 --> 00:01:52,282
And an Event Calendar is a simple calendar
that isn't tied to one team member.

30
00:01:52,282 --> 00:01:57,282
Use it for things like a treatment room,
or a piece of equipment that people book.

31
00:01:57,282 --> 00:01:59,842
Most businesses won't need one on day one.

32
00:02:00,693 --> 00:02:02,242
Let's close this for now.

33
00:02:02,242 --> 00:02:05,896
Back in the list, the type is
shown next to every calendar.

34
00:02:05,896 --> 00:02:09,923
Check-up and Clean is a round
robin, the open evening is a class,

35
00:02:09,923 --> 00:02:12,339
and the planning session is collective.

36
00:02:13,193 --> 00:02:14,684
Not sure which to pick?

37
00:02:14,684 --> 00:02:17,277
Ask one question: who needs to be there?

38
00:02:17,277 --> 00:02:20,194
If it's one specific
person, choose Personal.

39
00:02:20,194 --> 00:02:23,306
If anyone on a team will
do, choose Round Robin.

40
00:02:23,306 --> 00:02:27,066
If several people must attend
together, choose Collective.

41
00:02:27,066 --> 00:02:28,946
And for groups, choose Class.

42
00:02:29,798 --> 00:02:30,846
Here's a pro tip.

43
00:02:30,846 --> 00:02:35,347
Create one calendar per service, rather
than one calendar for everything.

44
00:02:35,347 --> 00:02:39,232
Different services need different
lengths, forms and reminders,

45
00:02:39,232 --> 00:02:42,561
and separate calendars make
your reports much clearer.

46
00:02:43,410 --> 00:02:44,732
Now you know the types!

47
00:02:44,732 --> 00:02:49,388
In the next lesson, we'll build a booking
calendar from scratch, with your hours,

48
00:02:49,388 --> 00:02:50,940
buffers and booking limits.

49
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:51,745
See you there.
